  "conclusions": [
    "The original coefficient field splits E, so its orthogonal idempotents concatenate the prescribed separate eigenspace bases over every K-algebra. This argument does not change any integral eigenlattice.",
    "The invariant-derivative exponential uses only factorial units and gives an addition- and coefficient-compatible isomorphism at every finite infinitesimal order. The smooth-section graded description works over arbitrary coefficient algebras, including nonnoetherian and nonreduced ones.",
    "The actual rigidified biextension frame lifts over the affine nilpotent jet thickenings by projective-module lifting and nilpotent Nakayama. Compatible units give an inverse-limit frame with both axis rigidifications.",
    "The original primitive graph transports the original line. The prior Good3 gauge construction divides only by integers and coefficient-field separability units, so it works over any K-algebra. The four canonical-gauge identities are preserved.",
    "Every actual section of every nonnegative line power has a compatible formal germ. IsNab quantifies only these powers; its integer-indexed NabV is correctly completed by zero on unused negative powers. Uniqueness treats every representative of a given germ.",
    "The harmonic change-of-gauge argument is an exact coefficient identity, with the original B(t,w0*t)=B(t,t)/2 normalization. It remains valid under arbitrary and nonflat base change; no canonical nonharmonic derivative is claimed.",
    "The original FrPt functor is the product of eigenspace frame bundles and the generator bundle of the already constructed theta pushforward line. It has finite presentation over K. Stacks 01ZM(2) descends each S-point through finitely generated subalgebras, which remain reduced when S is reduced; this gives the literal AllTest and FrMap clauses.",
    "The existing full Tate-marking comparison includes all original M and A labels even at shared prime powers. Compatible higher markings form a finite locally constant cover. The additional prescribed cyclotomic root can be reached while fixing all old labels because unramified or split principal-unit norms are surjective at the same depth.",
    "The forgetful natural transformation gives the original universal-family isomorphism and exact primitive-line, cube and rigidification comparison. The label factors are pd and A2/A, exactly as in DeltaDat.EtaOK.",
    "Each framed geometric point lifts with its exact tangent vectors and section generator, including the original local transition-frame equation in FrOver.",
    "For every n including zero the same cover works with c_delta=1 and phi_delta=1. The former has source weight (0,0) and value one at every framed geometric point. Every field of DeltaDat.IsLev is discharged on the prescribed l2,X2,c2."
  ],
